---
/**
 * ReadingProgress (DESIGN §5.18, M15, bepatrickdavid influence): an accent
 * hairline along the bottom edge of the sticky header that fills from left to
 * right as you scroll the page.
 *
 *   <ReadingProgress />          (once per page; ProjectLayout renders it)
 *
 * - Browsers with scroll-driven animations: pure CSS (animation-timeline:
 *   scroll(root)), works without JS.
 * - Others: scripts/project/reading-progress.ts writes --progress (0..1) on
 *   [data-reading-progress] from a passive scroll listener + rAF.
 * Kept under reduced motion: it is information, not decoration (it only
 *   moves when the user scrolls).
 * It sits ON the header's own 2px underline slot, so project pages never show
 * two accent lines; the header underline itself is not used on these pages.
 * Decorative for assistive tech (the scroll position already conveys it).
 */
---

<div class="reading-progress" data-reading-progress aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="reading-progress__bar"></span>
</div>

<style>
  .reading-progress {
    --rp-h: 2px;
    position: fixed;
    top: calc(var(--header-h) - var(--rp-h));
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    z-index: calc(var(--z-header) + 1); /* over the header's edge, under the menu */
    height: var(--rp-h);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .reading-progress__bar {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    background: var(--accent);
    transform: scaleX(var(--progress, 0));
    transform-origin: 0 50%;
  }

  @supports (animation-timeline: scroll()) {
    /* Longhands: older engines drop a whole shorthand that contains `auto`. */
    .reading-progress__bar {
      animation-name: reading-progress-fill;
      animation-duration: auto;
      animation-timing-function: linear;
      animation-fill-mode: both;
      animation-timeline: scroll(root block);
    }
  }

  @keyframes reading-progress-fill {
    from {
      transform: scaleX(0);
    }
    to {
      transform: scaleX(1);
    }
  }

  /* Hidden while the mobile menu covers the page. */
  :global(html.is-scroll-locked) .reading-progress {
    visibility: hidden;
  }
</style>
